A||||7||Lynx||Injectors will not fire.||||1||
Z||000000||Lynx||03-13-2001||09:32 PM||||I have a 85 GT and it has spark and i belive the fuel pump is good, you can hear it and if you hit the fuel valve on the fuel rail gas shoots up. The problem is it wont start and run. If you take a spray bottle full of gas and spay into the throttle body and start it, it will start and run if you keep spraying quickly. I belive that the injectors are not working, also there is not signal coming from the computer to turn on the fuel pump you have to hot wire the fuel pump. It seems like the computer? Has this happened to anybody, what are your suggestions?<P>Lynx<BR>I have never had a computer go out.||||reg||1
Z||000001||c m west||03-13-2001||09:45 PM||||well, it sounds as if you have had a computer go out - however, check BOTH injector fuses to see if they are blown<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||03-13-2001||10:09 PM||||I don't know about GM units, but ignition module is also possible culprit.||||reg||1
Z||000003||c m west||03-13-2001||10:15 PM||||In this particular case, the ignition module does not affect the injectors - check for a code 12 sequence in the ECM ( ground ALDL link terminals A and B ) to see if the ECM is functioning properly, then check too see if the injector fuses are blown, check fuel pressure, may just be the fuel pump, and check to see for blockage in the fuel filter<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||03-13-2001||10:16 PM||||After reviewing a few of my wiring diagrams, I am going back to my first instincts of fuses, fuseable link, or ignition module.<P>Lynx: you're from Roseburg?! It is very possible I will be moving out there this summer. I've been watching for Oregon members, never thought someone would be from Roseburg though. I was out there this past November or December, don't remember which, but is you're '85GT black, with dulling paint?<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 03-13-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000005||terryk||03-13-2001||10:21 PM||||Huh? The injectors are fired on ignition pulses.||||reg||1
Z||000006||filthyscarecrow||03-14-2001||12:01 AM||||i would guess it's the ECM. i had an 85GT that did that twice. had to replace the ECM both times. well, i sold it after it did it the second time... <BR>oh yeah CM WEST, terry is right. the ignition module DOES creat a reference pulse for the ECM to fire the injectors. don't believe me or him? check page 6E3-A-22 of the helm fiero manual. it's in #7 of the diagnosis. rpoblem could be in the pickup coil too, when was the last time that was replaced? <P>------------------<BR>allow me to show you my exhaust pipes...||||reg||1
Z||000007||DRH||03-14-2001||01:23 AM||||I doubt if it's the ignition module or pickup coil... seems either of those would keep it from running even when gas was sprayed in the throttle body. Check fuses and wiring connections before assuming it's the ECM. Also, check for codes as mentioned above.||||reg||1
